#. type: Title ##
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Solarpunk Manifesto"
msgstr "Manifest Solarpunka"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This manifesto was originally posted on re-des.org, which vanished from the "
"Internet in August 2025."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Many people have written about Solarpunk during the last 10+ years. Mostly "
"after 2014."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid "The genre is not yet clearly defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"This **Solarpunk Manifesto** is a creative re-adaptation of ideas about "
"solarpunk written by many people. These ideas can be mainly found in "
"_Solarpunk: a reference guide_ which can be found [here](https://medium.com/"
"solarpunks/solarpunk-a-reference-guide-8bcf18871965) and in _Solarpunk:_ "
"_Notes towards a Manifesto_ by Adam Flynn, which can be found [here](https://"
"hieroglyph.asu.edu/2014/09/solarpunk-notes-toward-a-manifesto/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk is a movement in speculative fiction, art, fashion, and activism "
"that seeks to answer and embody the question “what does a sustainable "
"civilization look like, and how can we get there?”"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The aesthetics of solarpunk merge the practical with the beautiful, the well-"
"designed with the green and lush, the bright and colorful with the earthy "
"and solid."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk can be utopian, just optimistic, or concerned with the struggles "
"en route to a better world , but never dystopian. As our world roils with "
"calamity, we need solutions, not only warnings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solutions to thrive without fossil fuels, to equitably manage real scarcity "
"and share in abundance instead of supporting false scarcity and false "
"abundance, to be kinder to each other and to the planet we share."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk is at once a vision of the future, a thoughtful provocation, a way "
"of living and a set of achievable proposals to get there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"We are solarpunks because optimism has been taken away from us and we are "
"trying to take it back."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid "We are solarpunks because the only other options are denial or despair."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"At its core, Solarpunk is a vision of a future that embodies the best of "
"what humanity can achieve: a post-scarcity, post-hierarchy, post-"
"capitalistic world where humanity sees itself as part of nature and clean "
"energy replaces fossil fuels."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The “punk” in Solarpunk is about rebellion, counterculture, post-capitalism, "
"decolonialism and enthusiasm. It is about going in a different direction "
"than the mainstream, which is increasingly going in a scary direction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk is a movement as much as it is a genre: it is not just about the "
"stories, it is also about how we can get there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '6.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk embraces a diversity of tactics: there is no single right way to "
"do solarpunk. Instead, diverse communities from around the world adopt the "
"name and the ideas, and build little nests of self-sustaining revolution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '7.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk provides a valuable new perspective, a paradigm and a vocabulary "
"through which to describe one possible future. Instead of embracing "
"retrofuturism, solarpunk looks completely to the future. Not an alternative "
"future, but a possible future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '8.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Our futurism is not nihilistic like cyberpunk and it avoids steampunk’s "
"potentially quasi-reactionary tendencies: it is about ingenuity, "
"generativity, independence, and community."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '9.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid "Solarpunk emphasizes environmental sustainability and social justice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '10.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk is about finding ways to make life more wonderful for us right "
"now, and also for the generations that follow us."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '11.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Our future must involve repurposing and creating new things from what we "
"already have. Imagine “smart cities” being junked in favor of smart "
"citizenry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '12.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk recognizes the historical influence politics and science fiction "
"have had on each other."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '13.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk recognizes science fiction as not just entertainment but as a form "
"of activism."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '14.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk wants to counter the scenarios of a dying earth, an insuperable "
"gap between rich and poor, and a society controlled by corporations. Not in "
"hundreds of years, but within reach."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '15.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk is about youth maker culture, local solutions, local energy grids, "
"ways of creating autonomous functioning systems. It is about loving the "
"world."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '16.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk culture includes all cultures, religions, abilities, sexes, "
"genders and sexual identities."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '17.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk is the idea of humanity achieving a social evolution that embraces "
"not just mere tolerance, but a more expansive compassion and acceptance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '18.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"The visual aesthetics of Solarpunk are open and evolving. As it stands, it "
"is a mash-up of the following: 1. 1800s age-of-sail/frontier living (but "
"with more bicycles) 2. Creative reuse of existing infrastructure (sometimes "
"post-apocalyptic, sometimes present-weird) 3. Appropriate technology 4. Art "
"Nouveau 5. Hayao Miyazaki 6. Jugaad-style innovation from the non-Western "
"world 7. High-tech backends with simple, elegant outputs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '19.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk is set in a future built according to principles of New Urbanism "
"or New Pedestrianism and environmental sustainability."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '20.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"Solarpunk envisions a built environment creatively adapted for solar gain, "
"amongst other things, using different technologies. The objective is to "
"promote self sufficiency and living within natural limits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '21.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid ""
"In Solarpunk we’ve pulled back just in time to stop the slow destruction of "
"our planet. We’ve learned to use science wisely, for the betterment of our "
"life conditions as part of our planet. We’re no longer overlords. We’re "
"caretakers. We’re gardeners."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '22.  '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "What is Solarpunk?"
msgid "Solarpunk:"
msgstr "Czym jest Solarpunk?"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid "is diverse"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid "has room for spirituality and science to coexist"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid "is beautiful"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#: content/essays/solarpunk-manifesto/index.en.md
msgid "can happen. Now."
msgstr ""

